I have a 1D vector called X that I want to train to be the same as
another 1D truth vector called Y given some input parameters P. I have
N such sets of parameters, truth vectors and vectors to be trained
(X,Y,P). How do I build a DNN in Matlab to do this?

You have N training examples, where for each example i:

P_i : input parameters (vector)
X_i : initial 1D vector you want to adjust/train
Y_i : target truth vector (desired output)

The DNN should learn to map (P, X) → Y (or a correction that makes X closer to Y).

Note " Sometimes more stable:
Target becomes Delta = Y - X
Network outputs correction → final = X + predicted_delta
Just change Target = Y - X; and keep everything else the same. This is often better when X is already close to Y.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

Recommended Approach: Concatenate P and X as Input
matlab% Data shapes (after organizing your data):

% P : [numParams × N]
% X : [vectorLength × N]     % initial vectors
% Y : [vectorLength × N]     % truth vectors

% Combine inputs
Input = [P; X];                % size: [numParams + vectorLength, N]
Target = Y;                    % size: [vectorLength, N]

% Strongly recommended: normalize
[InputNorm, muIn, sigmaIn] = normalize(Input, 2);   % along observations
[TargetNorm, muT, sigmaT]  = normalize(Target, 2);

% Optional: Split train/validation
idx = randperm(N);
trainIdx = idx(1:round(0.8*N));
valIdx   = idx(round(0.8*N)+1:end);

XTrain = InputNorm(:, trainIdx);
YTrain = TargetNorm(:, trainIdx);
XVal   = InputNorm(:, valIdx);
YVal   = TargetNorm(:, valIdx);

% Define network

numInputFeatures = size(Input, 1);   % = numParams + vectorLength
outputSize       = size(Y, 1);       % length of your 1D vector

layers = [
    featureInputLayer(numInputFeatures)
    
    fullyConnectedLayer(256)
    reluLayer
    batchNormalizationLayer
    
    fullyConnectedLayer(512)
    reluLayer
    batchNormalizationLayer
    
    fullyConnectedLayer(256)
    reluLayer
    batchNormalizationLayer
    
    fullyConnectedLayer(outputSize)
    % No activation (linear output) for regression
];

net = dlnetwork(layers);

% Training options

options = trainingOptions('adam', ...
    'MaxEpochs', 800, ...
    'MiniBatchSize', 32, ...           % adjust based on your N
    'InitialLearnRate', 1e-3, ...
    'LearnRateSchedule','piecewise', ...
    'LearnRateDropPeriod',200, ...
    'LearnRateDropFactor',0.5, ...
    'ValidationData',{XVal, YVal}, ...
    'ValidationFrequency',50, ...
    'Plots','training-progress', ...
    'Verbose',false);

%% train

net = trainnet(XTrain, YTrain, net, "mse", options);

%% Prediction/inference

% New sample: P_new and X_init_new
InputNew = [P_new; X_init_new];
InputNewNorm = (InputNew - muIn) ./ sigmaIn;   % use same stats

YpredNorm = predict(net, InputNewNorm);
Ypred     = YpredNorm .* sigmaT + muT;         % denormalize

